  ],
  "evidence": [
    "Pinned GraphicWin fills call original Buffer::copy5DFF00 directly at5D52F2 and5D53E6; current in-class header body expands into fills (297/324instructions versus original80/78). Existing GraphicWin runtime test covers sequencing, not original call boundaries.",
    "Commit85460a06b moved the existing seven-argument copy algorithm into buffer.h based on a PAU/PAV Flic COMDAT theory, then added anti-inline pointer-to-member spellings in Buffer wrappers/tile and Flic. Current Buffer is class-keyed throughout, Flic records PAV emitted symbol facts, and its struct-keyed trial was reverted. No original COFF/PDB evidence was found proving the historical duplicate-COMDAT theory. Catalogue names alone do not establish original linkage.",
    "Bounded candidate: move the SAME seven-argument copy body to its existing source mapping in buffer.cpp; leave its declaration and existing retention attributes in buffer.h. Restore ordinary calls at the3Buffer and4Flic sites whose comments tie PMFs to this body move. Keep get_data and other PMFs unchanged. Do not alter algorithm, quirks, lifetime, public ABI, class layout, flags, mappings or historical claims. Preserve useful historical evidence but replace assertions that the old inline placement is mandatory.",
    "Ownership subjects cover Buffer/Flic/GraphicWin for observation; editing authority is restricted to the copy boundary and its identified artificial call forms, plus actual-source tests. Do not opportunistically recover unrelated functions. Header consumers require fresh whole-source measurement or verified affected closure and full physical build comparison. Unexpected discoveries or outside-owner edits require coordinator expansion.",
    "Use native compiler overlays or an isolated prepared worker. Prove actual copied-body equivalence, original call targets and unchanged inputs/ordering. Require full build/link, relevant behavior tests, claim continuity and references. Preserve legitimate work and report matching regressions; never weaken gates, invent noinline/export/fake-reference hacks, or label scoped manual integration as game acceptance."
  ],
  "intent": "Restore the natural out-of-line Buffer copy boundary and remove source pointer-to-member workarounds introduced solely to suppress unintended inlining.",
